[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug: the parser reads dates month first. The reports
merged into it describe more than that. We read them by what they say and where they came from,
not by their subject line, and split the ticket. Each problem got its own ticket.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

<Callout>
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October. <code>parser</code> is fixed (<code>fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales</code>).
<code>hint</code> will not be fixed: the booking-v3 form is retired. <code>one-day</code> is not covered by either and stays open.
</Callout>

## The problems

**`parser`: the day and month are swapped.** The shared parser reads every date month first.
Every tenant on file writes the day first, so their dates come out flipped (7 April becomes
4 July). It comes in through the app, by email and through booking-v2's form. This is the bug the
queued fix is for.

**`hint`: the same swap, made by the form.** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date
field. The tenant's people type what the hint tells them, month first, and the form reads it the
tenant's way, day first. These reports look like the parser bug, but they come only through
booking-v3's form. The parser fix leaves them broken. The fix is the hint, not the parser.
Intake tagged reports by the reporter's browser, so its `hint` tag does not match this group:
the tenant and the form decide it.

**`one-day`: the date is one day off.** These reports show no swap. "Tuesday 12 May" arrives as
Monday 11 May; one meeting is Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto; an invite arrives before
the booking. That is a time-zone shift, not a day/month order. The desk read these reports this
way already (`desk-notes.json`). The desk counts them where their tenant files them, under
`parser`, so they show in both rows.

## Why they were merged

Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line alone. All three
problems arrive as "wrong date", so all three landed in one ticket. Same subject is not same cause:

<DedupeExplorer />

## Next time

- New wrong-date reports: check the tenant, the channel and the form before you merge. A
  booking-v3 form report goes to `hint`. A date one day off goes to `one-day`.
- Close each ticket when its own fix ships, or as not planned when engineering says it will not be fixed.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
